module test.fixture.dissolution_live_discriminator.subject

// THE INDEPENDENTLY AUTHORED SUBJECT PAIR for
// test.claim.dissolution_census_mechanism_witness_test's live discriminator. One
// declaration is authored here and one name is deliberately NOT, so the resolver's two
// answers — present and absent — are facts about this file rather than about whatever
// the corpus happens to contain on the day the witness runs.
//
// It is a fixture pool rather than a production pool root because the subject under test
// is the RESOLVER's behaviour, and scanning a production directory to establish it would
// price the mechanism at that directory's breadth. Measured: pointing the discriminator
// at dag/std cost a 2.6s index fill and the witness was budget-refused at 5510ms against
// the 5000ms deadline, undecided rather than failed.
//
// The absent half has no declaration by construction: `absent_subject_declaration` is
// named by the witness and authored nowhere, so adding it here would silently convert
// the discriminator's second arm into a duplicate of its first.
fn present_subject_declaration() -> Bool {
  true
}
